  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "chet-block-1",
      "sourceIndex": 0,
      "text": "Chet Hebrew Letter (ח): Sound, Furtive Patah & Practice",
      "reviewFlags": [],
      "type": "MAIN_TITLE"
    },
    {
      "id": "chet-block-2",
      "sourceIndex": 1,
      "text": "Chet (ח) is the eighth letter of the Hebrew alphabet. In common modern Hebrew pronunciation, its sound is similar to the ch in German 'Bach' or Scottish 'loch.' Let air flow continuously through a narrow space at the back of the mouth. In this lesson, ch represents this sound, rather than the English ch in 'chair.'",
      "reviewFlags": [],
      "type": "SIMPLE_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "chet-block-4",
      "sourceIndex": 3,
      "text": "Words to Practice:",
      "reviewFlags": [],
      "type": "SUBTITLE"
    },
    {
      "id": "chet-block-5",
      "sourceIndex": 4,
      "text": "brother",
      "reviewFlags": [],
      "type": "WORD_EXAMPLE",
      "word": "אָח",
      "transcription": "ach"
    },
    {
      "id": "chet-block-6",
      "sourceIndex": 5,
      "text": "The word אָח [ach] means 'brother' and has one syllable. Kamatz Gadol under Aleph (אָ) represents [a]. Chet at the end of the word (ח) supplies [ch]. There is no vowel sign under Chet in this word.",
      "reviewFlags": [],
      "type": "BOLD_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "chet-block-7",
      "sourceIndex": 6,
      "text": "holiday",
      "reviewFlags": [],
      "type": "WORD_EXAMPLE",
      "word": "חַג",
      "transcription": "chag"
    },
    {
      "id": "chet-block-8",
      "sourceIndex": 7,
      "text": "The word חַג [chag] means 'holiday' or 'festival' and has one syllable. It consists of Chet (ח) and Gimel (ג). Chet represents [ch]; with Patah beneath it (חַ), it is read [cha]. Gimel adds [g], giving [chag].",
      "reviewFlags": [],
      "type": "BOLD_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "chet-block-9",
      "sourceIndex": 8,
      "text": "Conclusions",
      "reviewFlags": [],
      "type": "SUBTITLE"
    },
    {
      "id": "chet-block-10",
      "sourceIndex": 9,
      "text": "Today, you learned the eighth letter of the Hebrew alphabet and expanded your vocabulary with two new words. You've made great progress—now it's time to practice and reinforce what you've learned.",
      "reviewFlags": [],
      "type": "SIMPLE_TEXT"
    }
  ],
